#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:3
msgid "How to Migrate from WebStorm to Zed"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:5
msgid ""
"This guide covers how to set up Zed if you're coming from WebStorm, "
"including keybindings, settings, and the differences you should expect as a "
"JavaScript/TypeScript developer."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:7
msgid "Install Zed"
msgstr "安裝 Zed"

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:9
msgid "Zed is available on macOS, Windows, and Linux."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:11
msgid ""
"For macOS, you can download it from zed.dev/download, or install via "
"Homebrew:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:17
msgid ""
"For Windows, download the installer from zed.dev/download, or install via "
"winget:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:23
msgid ""
"For most Linux users, the easiest way to install Zed is through our "
"installation script:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:29
msgid ""
"After installation, you can launch Zed from your Applications folder "
"(macOS), Start menu (Windows), or directly from the terminal using: `zed .` "
"This opens the current directory in Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:33
msgid "Set Up the JetBrains Keymap"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:35
msgid ""
"If you're coming from WebStorm, the fastest way to feel at home is to use "
"the JetBrains keymap. During onboarding, you can select it as your base "
"keymap. If you missed that step, you can change it anytime:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:37 src/migrate/webstorm.md:351
msgid "Open Settings with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-,\\|ctrl-,</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:38
msgid "Search for `Base Keymap`"
msgstr "搜尋 `Base Keymap`"

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:39
msgid "Select `JetBrains`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:41
msgid ""
"This maps familiar shortcuts like <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-o\\|ctrl-alt-"
"shift-n</kbd> for Go to Class and <kbd class=\"keybinding\">shift shift\\|"
"shift shift</kbd> for Find Action."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:43
msgid "Set Up Editor Preferences"
msgstr "設定編輯器偏好設定"

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:45
msgid ""
"You can configure most settings in the Settings Editor (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-,\\|ctrl-,</kbd>). For advanced settings, run `zed: "
"open settings file` from the Command Palette to edit your settings file "
"directly."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:47
msgid "Settings WebStorm users typically configure first:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:49
msgid "Zed Setting"
msgstr "Zed 設定"

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:49
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:51
msgid "`format_on_save`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:51
msgid "Auto-format when saving. Set to `\"on\"` to enable."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:52
msgid "`soft_wrap`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:52
msgid ""
"Wrap long lines. Options: `\"none\"`, `\"editor_width\"`, "
"`\"preferred_line_length\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:53
msgid "`preferred_line_length`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:53
msgid "Column width for wrapping and rulers. Default is 80."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:54
msgid "`inlay_hints`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:54
msgid "Show parameter names and type hints inline, like WebStorm's hints."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:55
msgid "`relative_line_numbers`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:55
msgid "Useful if you're coming from IdeaVim."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:57
msgid ""
"Zed also supports per-project settings. Create a `.zed/settings.json` file "
"in your project root to override global settings for that project, similar "
"to how you might use `.idea` folders in WebStorm."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:59
msgid ""
"**Tip:** If you're joining an existing project, check `format_on_save` "
"before making your first commit. Otherwise you might accidentally reformat "
"an entire file when you only meant to change one line."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:61
msgid "Open or Create a Project"
msgstr "開啟或建立專案"

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:63
msgid ""
"After setup, use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-n\\|ctrl-alt-n</kbd> to "
"open a folder. This becomes your workspace in Zed. Unlike WebStorm, there's "
"no project configuration wizard, no framework selection dialog, and no "
"project structure setup required."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:65
msgid ""
"To start a new project, create a directory using your terminal or file "
"manager, then open it in Zed. The editor will treat that folder as the root "
"of your project. For new projects, you'd typically run `npm init`, `pnpm "
"create`, or your framework's CLI tool first, then open the resulting folder "
"in Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:67
msgid ""
"You can also launch Zed from the terminal inside any folder with: `zed .`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:70
msgid "Once inside a project:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:72
msgid ""
"Use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-n\\|ctrl-alt-n</kbd> to jump between "
"files quickly (like WebStorm's \"Recent Files\")"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:73
msgid ""
"Use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">shift shift\\|shift shift</kbd> to open the "
"Command Palette (like WebStorm's \"Search Everywhere\")"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:74
msgid ""
"Use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-o\\|ctrl-alt-shift-n</kbd> to search for "
"symbols (like WebStorm's \"Go to Symbol\")"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:76
msgid ""
"Open buffers appear as tabs across the top. The Project Panel shows your "
"file tree and Git status. Toggle it with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-1\\|"
"alt-1</kbd> (just like WebStorm's Project tool window)."
msgstr ""

