msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:205
msgid ""
"Use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">shift-f10\\|shift-f10</kbd> to run tasks "
"quickly"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:206
msgid ""
"Lean on your terminal (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">alt-f12\\|alt-f12</kbd>) "
"for anything tasks don't cover"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:208
msgid "No Framework Integration"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:210
msgid ""
"WebStorm's value for web development comes largely from its framework "
"integration. React components get special treatment. Angular has dedicated "
"tooling. Vue single-file components are fully understood. The npm tool "
"window shows all your scripts."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:212
msgid ""
"Zed has none of this built-in. The TypeScript language server sees your code "
"as TypeScript—it doesn't understand that a function is a React component or "
"that a file is an Angular service."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:216
msgid ""
"Use grep and file search liberally. <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-h\\|"
"ctrl-shift-h</kbd> with a regex can find component definitions, route "
"configurations, or API endpoints."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:217
msgid ""
"Rely on your language server's \"find references\" (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-f7\\|ctrl-alt-f7</kbd>) for navigation—it "
"works, just without framework context"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:218
msgid ""
"Consider using framework-specific CLI tools (`ng`, `next`, `vite`) from "
"Zed's terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:219
msgid ""
"For React, JSX/TSX syntax and TypeScript types still provide good "
"intelligence"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:221
msgid ""
"**Tip:** For projects with complex configurations, keep your framework's "
"documentation handy. Zed's speed comes with less hand-holding for framework-"
"specific features."
msgstr ""

